  "readings": {
    "main_front_reference": "Source rays at Y=0 place the rear of the warm-grey underside primarily from Z10.39 to 10.64. The working common level is 10.52. The lowest visible laneside underside falls to Z9.72 (about 0.8m at 7.1m depth); winter obliques carry greater scale error at the far east edge.",
    "eave_corner_uncertainty": "Five-station loss soft_l1 solution varies with tree and mobile-panorama parallax. In particular the 2015 western station point is partly covered by a branch (up to ~18px). The February 2018 crop cuts off this outer corner above the image.",
    "terrace": "Left/east of the stepped roof the 2018 and 2020 images show a separate pale folded cap on a short terrace front from X−8.72 to approximately −5.65. The sheltered short eave behind it is sampled, but its concealed windows and roof extension are unresolved.",
    "painted_stack": "2018 original resolves two white square heads, round pipe, lower side branch, multiple collars, a slanted top offset beneath the gutter and the disappearance behind the lane pier. Native pipe points in panorama closeups can deviate by 4–14 px from the common registered solution. The original image is the detailed support for component positioning on the near-side wall.",
    "roof": "2019 and 2025 ortho imagery resolved a paired diagonal in the lane-end outer roof section. Individually rectified apexes about 2.8–3.5m behind the street eaves and 4.5–5.1m from lane. Far edge 7.8–10.2m is approximate; model is clipped at the separately photographed 7.1m section. Apex height 12.06 is conditional on a 17–23 degree pitch. The far fold and its height are schematic; no separate rear or neighbouring structure is included."
  }
}
